# Every path is owned by the human editors. Never list a bot, GitHub App or agent account here.
# The main-branch ruleset requires a pull request and the "validate" check, but no approvals: the editor
# opens most PRs, and GitHub doesn't let anyone approve their own. So this file asks the editors for review;
# it doesn't block a merge. Once a second person or a separate agent account exists, turn on
# "Require review from Code Owners" and "Require approval of the most recent push" in the ruleset.
# Editors are managed in the org team; add or remove people there, not in this file.
*                       @Alabama-Ballot-Guide/editors

# Content (agents may propose changes here; a human must approve)
/data.js                @Alabama-Ballot-Guide/editors

# Voter-service facts lock, source allowlist and validator: humans only, never in an agent PR
/security/              @Alabama-Ballot-Guide/editors
/scripts/               @Alabama-Ballot-Guide/editors

# Build, page code, crawler files and CI
/.github/               @Alabama-Ballot-Guide/editors
/build.py               @Alabama-Ballot-Guide/editors
/gen.js                 @Alabama-Ballot-Guide/editors
/app.js                 @Alabama-Ballot-Guide/editors
/shell.html             @Alabama-Ballot-Guide/editors
/og-card.html           @Alabama-Ballot-Guide/editors
/package.json           @Alabama-Ballot-Guide/editors
/package-lock.json      @Alabama-Ballot-Guide/editors
